      "sentence_id": 15,
      "text": "// 2 // Learned counsel for the petitioners submitted that the revision petition has been filed challenging the judgment and order dated 04.02.2010 passed by the learned Nyayadhikari, Puri in G.R. Case No.1233 of 2005 /T.R. No.126/2009 in convicting the petitioners under sections Narana @ Narayan vs State Of Odisha .... Opp. Party on 22 March, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/165788359/\n1 323/341/34 of the Indian Penal Code and sentenced them to pay a fine of Rs.600/-(Rupees six hundred) each, in default, to undergo S.I. for a period of twenty days for the offence under section 323 of the Indian Penal Code and to pay a fine of Rs.200/- (rupees two hundred) each, in default, to undergo S.I. for a period of five days for the offence under section 341 of the Indian Penal Code.\nSection 376 Cr.P.C. which deals with no appeal in petty cases indicates that the appeal by a convicted person will not be maintainable if a Magistrate of the First Class passes only a sentence of fine not exceeding one hundred rupees.",
